From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: sunxi: a733: Count port K among the interrupt banks

The A733 binding lists eleven interrupts, a placeholder for the absent
port A and one each for ports B to K, and the interrupt banks are
numbered by port, so port K is bank 10. With ten banks, port K gets no
parent interrupt and the probe writes its irq_array entries past the
end of the array. Declare eleven banks; the port K interrupt registers
at 0x5c0 follow the regular bank stride.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; edge detection on PK0
through the GPIO character device works, where it failed with ENXIO before,
and PB0 still works.

Fixes: 0535bfbfa97b ("pinctrl: sunxi: add support for the Allwinner A733")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c
index ca82f08a3a65..bc483d983bbc 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/sunxi/pinctrl-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@ static const u8 a733_irq_bank_muxes[SUNXI_PINCTRL_MAX_BANKS] =
 	{  0, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14, 14};
 
 static struct sunxi_pinctrl_desc a733_pinctrl_data = {
-	.irq_banks = 10,
+	.irq_banks = 11,
 	.irq_read_needs_mux = true,
 	.io_bias_cfg_variant = BIAS_VOLTAGE_PIO_POW_MODE_SEL,
 };
